1. Derived from Herdr (Apache License 2.0)
------------------------------------------

Herdr is developed by herdrdev (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr-app) and is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0, the same license as this repository. Herdr's own layouts and mods are shipped with the app, readable on
every installation, and the Herdr documentation tells people to clone them (`layout.clone`, `mod.clone`) and edit the
clones. Redistributing such clones is allowed under the Apache License 2.0 provided this notice and the statement of
changes below travel with them. Each clone records its source in its `cloned_from` field.

Modified copies (all taken from Herdr 0.1.12):

  layouts/portrait.json            from the layout `main`
  layouts/portrait-bottom.json     from the layout `main`
      Changes: new node tree (a full-width bar of space columns above or below the work area, a tab strip, a hidden
      right panel with Files and Changes); the sidebar, the Spaces and Agents lists and the Vault child removed; no theme
      pinned; root `preview` field added.
  mods/portrait-tabs/             from the mod `tabs`
      Changes: the Files and Changes buttons moved to mods/bar-strip; the per-space memory of the right panel kept
      here; the optional Vault panel allowed; icons copied into the mod; assets renamed to the new folder.
  mods/portrait-pane/             from the mod `pane`
      Changes: shows a note's name and folder for panes of the optional Vault reader; icons copied into the mod; assets
      renamed to the new folder.
  mods/portrait-files/            from the mod `files`
      Changes: a click on a file opens it in nvim in a floating window (mods/nvim-float) instead of a preview, with
      the read-only preview kept for Alt-click and for Windows; a title was added to mod.json.

Not redistributed: Herdr's other mods (`workspace-status`, `changes`, `picker`, `machine-add`, `menu`, `new-menu`)
are only used by name; they come with the person's Herdr and are never copied into this repository.


2. Icons copied from Herdr 0.1.12 (Apache License 2.0; glyphs: Lucide, ISC, and MIT)
